        {
          "id": 1354267490,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Might need to check for `__INTEL_LLVM_COMPILER` as well. The old (\"Classic\") Intel Compiler defines `__INTEL_COMPILER` but the new LLVM based one does not (but does define __GNUC__ but I think not __clang):\n\nhttps://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/articles/technical/use-predefined-macros-for-specific-code-for-intel-dpcpp-compiler-intel-cpp-compiler-intel-cpp-compiler-classic.html\n\nhttps://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/dpcpp-cpp-compiler/developer-guide-reference/2023-0/additional-predefined-macros.html",
